* Screen library: ask for the cursor lock for the program that reads its keys through the library.
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 18 Oct 26 dm  New (terminal 140 by 42, phase 3).
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L1 (R-b): VAR.ARGS; the layout mode (a fourth argument 'layout', the layout's size fifth and sixth), in which the WINDOW decides:
*               the lock holds while the window is smaller than minw by minh (the app's floor) and lifts as soon as it is not, wherever the cursor
*               is.  The three-argument call keeps the cursor mode exactly as it was.  A layout re-arm of the app that already
*               holds the lock keeps its "user chose to leave".
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.134: CED asks for the layout mode too, so no program of SD's own uses the three-argument cursor mode now; the mode itself is unchanged.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_guardmode(name, minw, minh {, mode, layw, layh})
*
*     name        what the program is called in the warning (IDE); null takes the lock off
*     minw minh   the cursor mode: the size the program is laid out for.  The layout mode: the program's FLOOR, the smallest window it is laid out for
*     mode        optional: 'layout' for the layout mode; left out or null, the cursor mode
*     layw layh   optional, the layout mode: the size the program is laid out at now ($tk_layout passes ctx<TK.C.W> and ctx<TK.C.H>); kept with the lock
*                 for the program's own use, not part of the test (a page whose layout follows the window is laid out at the window's size whenever the
*                 window is at least the floor, so "smaller than the layout" and "smaller than the floor" are one test once the page has made its
*                 layout again; a page that has not done so yet must not be locked and unlocked in turn on every redraw)
*
*   THE CURSOR MODE (the three-argument call; none of SD's own programs uses it since 9 Nov 26, when CED joined the IDE in the layout mode).  A full-screen program that reads its keys through the library is laid out for 140 by 42 and shows
*   the upper left corner of the layout when the window is smaller.  So long as the cursor ($sl_curat) is in the part that shows that is
*   safe; when it is not, $sl_key does not hand the program a key but takes the keyboard itself ($sl_guard: a warning in the upper
*   left, every key dropped, Ctrl-Q the one way out) until the window is made bigger.
*
*   THE LAYOUT MODE (28 Oct 2026, the toolkit's pages through $tk_layout).  The cursor of a page waits at the start of its status line, which
*   fits a window too narrow or a row or two too short for the page, so the cursor could not tell: $sl_key takes the keyboard whenever the
*   window is smaller than the floor (message 12545, naming the floor) and gives it back as soon as the window is the floor or larger.
*
*   In both modes Ctrl-Q, then y, makes $sl_key hand back the key 'guardquit' from then on (and the dialogues of the library read it as Esc),
*   which the program turns into leaving without saving.  SCREEN CLOSE and $sl_cleanup take the lock off, so it never reaches the next program;
*   a user's SCREEN OPEN program does not ask for it, so SD imposes nothing on it.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_guardmode(name, minw, minh, mode, layw, layh) var.args
$catalog $sl_guardmode

   common /slguard/ g.on, g.name, g.minw, g.minh, g.quit, g.mode, g.lw, g.lh

   md = ''
   if not(unassigned(mode)) then md = mode
   lw = ''
   lh = ''
   if not(unassigned(layw)) then lw = layw
   if not(unassigned(layh)) then lh = layh

   * a re-arm in the layout mode for the app that holds the lock (a resize, $tk_layout 'refresh') keeps the user's choice to leave
   keep.quit = 0
   if md = 'layout' and name # '' then
      if g.on and g.mode = 'layout' and g.name = name then keep.quit = 1
   end
   if not(keep.quit) then g.quit = 0

   if name = '' then
      g.on = 0
      g.mode = ''
      g.lw = ''
      g.lh = ''
   end else
      g.on = 1
      g.name = name
      g.minw = minw
      g.minh = minh
      g.mode = ''
      g.lw = ''
      g.lh = ''
      if md = 'layout' then
         g.mode = 'layout'
         g.lw = lw
         g.lh = lh
      end
   end

   return
end

* END-CODE
